{"author":"Michael Giver","author_email":"mikegiver@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"PR OPENED 2026-07-29 as DRAFT: https://github.com/navapbc/oscer/pull/822 (Part of #805, base main). Five commits: b411fb54 wiring, 46c84c32 email re-key, c9003b2e comment corrections, ad7da507 shared assessment + spec helpers, ff257ffc comment trim. mergeable=MERGEABLE (no conflict with #821, which landed on main first); CI running at open.\n\nPR body written independently of the commit messages and reframed on review feedback: the Context section describes where the work sits in epic #732 (contract #754, VA adapter #755, registry #756, exclusion-path consultation #808, provenance #811, ordering engine #812 which nothing consumed) rather than defending choices. The earlier draft read as a list of deviations, but most of those were just the expected design; the FEATURE_MOCK_DATA_SOURCES note and the determination-shape rationale were dropped for that reason.\n\nNOT in the PR body, by decision: the three reviewer questions (exception-wins precedence when one source emits both outcome kinds; dashboard income-cards default for data_source_ce rows, hidden by income_summary_visible?'s allow-list; attempted retained unconsumed). All three are documented in code. Raise them as a PR comment or in #tss-oscer if they should be actively asked.\n\nSTILL OPEN: (1) do NOT let GitHub default the squash message to b411fb54 -- its body still describes the mock firing on an odd va_icn last digit, superseded by 46c84c32. (2) Four unticketed gaps need issues or #810 widened: errored source yields a member-facing not_compliant row indistinguishable from a clean negative; an error outside expected_error_classes is swallowed by Strata's rescue Exception and strands the case; an order-bearing hybrid source stalls the same way; and the missing ExternalException.enabled? gate has no ticket at all."},"env_id":"7fda8af9-5f39-45e1-9caf-59ffda62ec19","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785340345800308001,"uuid":"33e5a3c3-0fc9-4116-8aec-2f8db2184296"}